WEBVTT

00:00:05.781 --> 00:00:11.652
A group collects neighboring records with the same value. Add a heading for each group and a subtotal in its footer.

00:00:16.832 --> 00:00:23.942
Open the fictional Regional Sales grouping practice report. It has a short sales list with region, city and amount fields.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:34.636
In the Structure explorer, choose Add, then Group. Pick the sales list and group it by region.

00:00:36.681 --> 00:00:42.734
Name the group Region, sort it alphabetically, and repeat its header if the group continues on another page.

00:00:53.703 --> 00:00:59.857
The new group gets header and footer bands. Add a formula in the header so each section displays its region name.

00:01:13.032 --> 00:01:20.065
In the group footer, calculate the total for only this region with sumBy over group.rows. Format the result as currency.

00:01:25.107 --> 00:01:31.235
Preview the report. Verify that cities sit under the right region and each regional total follows its group.

00:01:33.417 --> 00:01:40.465
The same pattern works for customers, product families, departments or any data field that defines a useful section.
